      {
        "id": 60720,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-21T03:57:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yep, you don't have to pay for it, and you don't have to wait for it to cycle through your deck.</p><p>I have seen similar namings on other cards. So not entirely sure which one is correct.</p><p>Now, consider this. Boarding Party is a Boost without phase limitations. Therefore, you could theoretically play it before moving in the travel phase, ping a ship, install a Tech from that Sector, and move to another sector to buy stuff. If you do this however, you don;t get the money. You can of course use it after the Requisition phase and get the money, ping, the ship, etc in the new Sector. Just showing you how some of the ideas work together, and some of the decisions you have to make.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:36:50.632Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 7769,
        "topic_slug": "blue-credit-symbol-on-station-cards",
        "display_username": "Pydro",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
